  "Question": "Which statement is correct?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "If \\(x\\lt0,\\) then \\(x^2\\gt x.\\)",
    "B": "If \\(x^2\\gt0,\\) then \\(x\\gt0.\\)",
    "C": "If \\(x^2\\gt x,\\) then \\(x\\gt0.\\)",
    "D": "If \\(x^2\\gt x,\\) then \\(x\\lt0.\\)",
    "E": "If \\(x\\lt1,\\) then \\(x^2\\lt x.\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "A square is nonnegative. Consequently, whenever \\(x<0\\),\n\\[\nx^2\\ge0>x,\n\\]\nwhich proves A for every value satisfying its hypothesis.\n\nTo check the other statements, take \\(x=-1\\). Then \\(x^2=1>0\\), \\(x^2>x\\), and \\(x<1\\), but both \\(x>0\\) and \\(x^2<x\\) are false. Thus B, C, and E each have a true hypothesis and a false conclusion at \\(x=-1\\).\n\nFor D, take \\(x=2\\). Its hypothesis \\(x^2>x\\) is true because \\(4>2\\), but its conclusion \\(x<0\\) is false. Therefore the correct statement is A.",
